.TH CCOL_CIRCQ_TRY_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_circq_try_send_zc \- try to send a message with no block
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_circq_try_send_zc(ccol_circular_queue *cq, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Puts the message into the queue if there is room, and returns
ccol_container_full at once when the queue is full. On success the
ownership of msg->data moves to the queue.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cq   Circular queue to send to
msg  Message to send. On success the ownership of the data moves to the
     queue.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success         - The message was sent
ccol_invalid_args    - cq or msg is NULL, msg->data is NULL while
                       msg->size is not 0, or msg->data is not NULL
                       while msg->size is 0
ccol_not_permitted   - Sends on the queue are turned off
ccol_container_full  - The queue is full
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This call never blocks. On failure the caller keeps the ownership of
msg->data.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_circq_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_circq_timed_send_zc (3)
